/**
 * Grade 12 informational articles: 50 of them, five for each of RI.11-12.1
 * to RI.11-12.10, alternating science and social studies.
 *
 * Held to the bands in scripts/reading-article-plan.json: eight or nine
 * paragraphs, a higher version at LL 1280-1400 and a lower one at LL
 * 1050-1160 with the same lettered paragraphs. These are written at nine
 * throughout, which is the only grade that uses the upper figure.
 *
 * The standards are the same ten as grade 11, so the difference is in the
 * material. Grade 11 took RI.11-12.9 through five foundational documents
 * less often taught than the ones grades 9 and 10 had used. This grade
 * takes five more, and includes the case that makes the standard's phrase
 * about rhetorical features hardest to apply honestly: a speech that
 * survives in two versions, twelve years apart, where the famous one was
 * reconstructed by somebody else.
 *
 * RI.11-12.8 again takes legal reasoning and public advocacy. Grade 11
 * used Marbury, Harlan, Jackson, Federalist 51 and Brown. This grade uses
 * McCulloch, the Korematsu dissents, Gideon, Cooper Union and Federalist
 * 78, which between them cover implied powers, a judgment the Court has
 * since repudiated, a case begun by a pencilled letter, a campaign speech
 * built on archival research, and the argument for judicial power made
 * before any court had claimed it.
 *
 *   bun run scripts/articles/g12.src.mjs && bun run scripts/merge-articles.mjs
 *   bun run scripts/check-articles.mjs
 */
