      "In the 1820s a tunnel was begun beneath a tidal river in a city, which had not been done under a navigable waterway anywhere. The ground was soft, waterlogged and in places barely coherent, and the mining methods of the day were useless in it.",
      "The method that made it possible was taken from an animal. A shipworm bores through submerged timber by advancing behind a hard shell that protects the part doing the cutting, and an engineer who had examined one patented a frame working on the same principle.",
      "The frame was a grid of cells, each holding one man facing the clay. A worker took out a board, cut back a few inches, replaced the board, and when every cell had advanced the whole frame was screwed forward while bricklayers lined the space behind it.",
