      "It worked, and it did not work reliably. The river broke in repeatedly, the worst inundation killing six men and nearly drowning the engineer's son, who was in the workings when the water came through and was carried out on the flood.",
      "The project then stopped for seven years for want of money, with the workings sealed and the shaft standing open in the middle of a city. The halt was financial rather than technical, which is the usual reason large works stop and is rarely the reason they are remembered.",
      "It opened in 1843 as a foot tunnel and became an attraction rather than a thoroughfare. Crowds came to walk under the river, stalls were set up in the arches, and the commercial purpose for which it had been dug was never achieved.",
